$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(2-Naphthyl)benzaldehyde. A dioxane/water solution (60 mL, 4:1) of
o-iodobenzaldehyde (929 mg, 5.02 mmol), 2-naphthylboronic acid (1.03 g,
6.02 mmol), tetrakis(triphenylphosphine) palladium (173 mg, 3 mol%), and
potassium carbonate (1.45 g, 10.5 mmol) was refluxed for 13 h. An aqueous
saturated ammonium chloride was then added. Organic materials were
extracted with ether three times. The combined extracts were washed with
brine and dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate. After removal of the
solvent under reduced pressure, the residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (hexane/ethyl acetate 10:1).
2-(2-naphthyl)benzaldehyde (1.11 g, 91%) as a colorless liquid.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
